---

[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '“Spatial Capture” is one of the truly unique new&nbsp; features of the Insta360 X6 and the Insta360 app.&nbsp;&nbsp; With Spatial Capture, you can create a 3D model&nbsp; of a large object, a room, or a space—such as a&nbsp;&nbsp; garden. You can then move around freely and look&nbsp; around inside this 3D model. This is not only&nbsp;&nbsp; great for virtual tours but also offers a whole&nbsp; new way to preserve memories. Today I’ll show you&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'how this feature works and what you need to keep&nbsp; in mind to create the best 3D models. By the way,&nbsp;&nbsp; Spatial Capture also works with the X5 and&nbsp; X4Air. The only important thing is that the&nbsp;&nbsp; app and the cameras\' firmware are up to date. Spatial Capture is based on 3D Gaussian Splatting,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a 3D rendering technique that can&nbsp; very efficiently convert videos and&nbsp;&nbsp; photos into 3D models. Until now, however,&nbsp; this was somewhat cumbersome and required&nbsp;&nbsp; specialized software. With Spatial Capture&nbsp; and the X6, though, it’s relatively simple.&nbsp;'

[00:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Creating a 3D model with Spatial Capture starts&nbsp; with a recording. You’ll need to use the X6&nbsp;&nbsp; in 360 Video mode and should shoot in 8K at 30&nbsp; frames per second. Recording in Pure Video mode&nbsp;&nbsp; is also possible. It’s important that you have&nbsp; the standard color profile enabled. Recording&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in I-Log won’t work. The video must be between 30&nbsp; seconds and 2 minutes long and must be uploaded to&nbsp;&nbsp; the cloud. For good results, keep the following in&nbsp; mind when recording: the feature is only suitable&nbsp;&nbsp; for static objects—not for people or cars that are&nbsp; moving. It works better when lighting conditions&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are good—so recording in low light is generally&nbsp; not recommended, even though it works in Pure&nbsp;&nbsp; Video mode. Spatial Capture has difficulty&nbsp; when there are different heights—for example,&nbsp;&nbsp; if you want to capture a house with multiple&nbsp; floor levels. This is challenging anyway given&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the 2-minute time limit. When capturing a house,&nbsp; you should therefore limit yourself to individual&nbsp;&nbsp; floor levels. Significant changes in lighting&nbsp; conditions are also not ideal—that is, scenarios&nbsp;&nbsp; where there are very bright and very dark areas. Before you begin, you should decide which area you&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'want to convert into a 3D model. I’m taking a shot&nbsp; here in the garden, but not the entire garden—I’ve&nbsp;&nbsp; already decided which part of the garden I want&nbsp; to capture. Now you should hold the camera as&nbsp;&nbsp; follows. Use the X6 on a selfie stick and hold&nbsp; it about half a meter above your head. The lenses&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'should be facing left and right. Depending on the&nbsp; situation, this might be too high—for example,&nbsp;&nbsp; inside a room. Alternatively, you can hold the&nbsp; camera in front of you at chest height. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp; you should slowly walk through the area you want&nbsp; to scan—a little slower than you would normally&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'walk. It’s important to keep the camera steady&nbsp; and avoid making any sudden movements. Move in&nbsp;&nbsp; circular patterns through the area you want to&nbsp; scan several times. As you walk through it again,&nbsp;&nbsp; you should adjust the height at which you hold the&nbsp; camera to capture as much as possible. To capture&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the ceiling and floor, you should also take&nbsp; a shot where you hold the X6 straight forward&nbsp;&nbsp; with the lenses facing up and down. If you want&nbsp; to capture a specific object in great detail,&nbsp;&nbsp; you can circle it several times while pointing&nbsp; the camera toward the object. Everything must be&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'included in a single recording. And don’t&nbsp; forget—it can’t be longer than 2 minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp; Once you’ve finished recording, you’ll need to&nbsp; upload the file to the cloud. There are several&nbsp;&nbsp; ways to do this: either you’ve enabled automatic&nbsp; backup, in which case it happens automatically—for&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[02:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'example, when you plug the camera in to charge—or&nbsp; you select the shot from the camera’s album and&nbsp;&nbsp; tap the “Upload to the Cloud” icon at the&nbsp; bottom. Now there’s just one final step:&nbsp;&nbsp; Open the Insta360 app, select the album,&nbsp; and then tap “Cloud.” In the row below,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can then select “Spatial Capture.” Tap the&nbsp; plus sign and then select your clip. The 3D&nbsp;&nbsp; rendering now takes place entirely in the cloud,&nbsp; and you don’t need to keep the app open for it.&nbsp;&nbsp; The process can take about an hour. You’ll&nbsp; then find the result here in the overview;&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can open it and move around and look&nbsp; around inside your newly created 3D model.&nbsp; In the top-right corner, you can switch between&nbsp; a horizontal landscape orientation and a portrait&nbsp;&nbsp; view. There’s a joystick mode that lets you move&nbsp; around and look around inside the model using&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these two control pads. Or a gyro mode, which lets&nbsp; you look around by moving your phone. In addition&nbsp;&nbsp; to Spatial, there are two other views—Ripple and&nbsp; Particle—that play a pre-made futuristic video of&nbsp;&nbsp; the captured space. Let’s say you want to embed&nbsp; the model on a website or share it with others;&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[03:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'right now, you can do that via a link. This link&nbsp; will open the model in a browser, and anyone who&nbsp;&nbsp; opens the link can look around inside your model&nbsp; just like here in the app. This also works on a&nbsp;&nbsp; desktop, where you can navigate the model using&nbsp; the keyboard and mouse, similar to a video game.&nbsp;'

[04:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Spatial Capture is currently still in beta and&nbsp; will certainly be significantly improved over&nbsp;&nbsp; time. Depending on how well you captured the&nbsp; environment, the result might still look a bit&nbsp;&nbsp; pixelated. It’s definitely not super sharp yet.&nbsp; Clear structures, such as buildings or rooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'work much better than when there are a lot&nbsp; of small details, like here in the garden.&nbsp; There are also no additional features at the&nbsp; moment, and Spatial Capture isn’t yet available in&nbsp;&nbsp; the U.S. for technical reasons. But I think it’s a&nbsp; cool and useful new feature. And of course, you’ll&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'need a cloud subscription to use it—after all,&nbsp; you have to upload your recordings to the cloud.&nbsp;&nbsp; There’s currently an interesting offer available&nbsp; for this. If you’re interested in the X6, you’ll&nbsp;&nbsp; find a link to it in the description below. If you&nbsp; use this link, you’ll not only receive a Double&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[04:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Lens Kit to replace two damaged lenses, but also&nbsp; 500GB of free cloud storage for one year. And that&nbsp;&nbsp; should be enough to create plenty of 3D models.&nbsp; But this offer is for a limited time only and&nbsp;&nbsp; is available exclusively through the link in the&nbsp; description. Let me know in the comments if you&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have any further questions. And give me a like&nbsp; as feedback if you found the video interesting&nbsp;&nbsp; or helpful. There will be more videos about the X6&nbsp; coming soon. So stay tuned, and see you next time!'
